{
 "title": "VAE (8×8 digits)",
 "description": "The variational version of Autoencoder (8×8 digits), from the same lecture: the same layers, except that the encoder ends in two heads, the mean μ and the log-variance log σ² of a 2-dimensional Gaussian code. z = μ + ε·exp(½·log σ²), with ε from a Noise node (the reparameterization trick, so gradients reach μ and σ). The loss is the negative evidence lower bound: binary cross-entropy summed over the 64 pixels plus the KL divergence of the code's Gaussian from N(0, 1). To generate, skip the encoder: draw z from N(0, 1) and decode. 33,604 parameters.",
